WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:02.141
- There was this girl I had a
huge crush on when I was a kid

00:00:02.141 --> 00:00:04.242
and she wore this like
cotton candy perfume,

00:00:04.242 --> 00:00:05.833
and every time I would smell it,

00:00:05.833 --> 00:00:07.202
I would, like, think about her,

00:00:07.202 --> 00:00:09.873
and then a couple years later,
my sister started wearing it

00:00:09.873 --> 00:00:12.322
and that, that (bleep) me up.

00:00:12.322 --> 00:00:17.322
(upbeat music)

00:00:30.432 --> 00:00:31.843
- Ugh.

00:00:31.872 --> 00:00:32.850
- This smells kind of lemony,

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:34.482
with a hint of rose.

00:00:34.488 --> 00:00:35.230
- I'm not mad at that,

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:36.971
that smells kind of like candy I think.

00:00:36.971 --> 00:00:38.550
- It smells like you
would clean with this.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:40.350
- I don't know man, all
perfume smells like,

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:41.801
they smell like moms to me.

00:00:41.801 --> 00:00:43.786
- You know in the bathroom,
when someone just blew it up

00:00:43.786 --> 00:00:45.400
and they Febreeze it?

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:46.967
Kinda getting that hint right now.

00:00:46.967 --> 00:00:48.569
- I feel like I could
smell this on a guy, too,

00:00:48.569 --> 00:00:50.345
and still be like, "Alright,
this works for you."

00:00:50.345 --> 00:00:51.901
- I can't imagine getting
a whiff of this at a bar

00:00:51.901 --> 00:00:54.135
and being like, "Ooh, who's that?"

00:00:54.135 --> 00:00:56.375
This is more like, "Oh
shit, mom came to pick me up

00:00:56.375 --> 00:00:57.815
"because I got too drunk."

00:00:57.815 --> 00:01:00.811
(upbeat music)

00:01:00.811 --> 00:01:02.551
I don't know what gold
smells like, but this isn't

00:01:02.551 --> 00:01:04.294
what I pictured gold smelling like.

00:01:04.294 --> 00:01:06.430
- This one kind of smells
like marshmallows and vodka.

00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:07.555
- Birthday cake.

00:01:07.555 --> 00:01:09.749
- This one smells like Off mosquito spray.

00:01:09.749 --> 00:01:12.617
- I could see a Kardashian
wearing this one, but not Kim.

00:01:12.617 --> 00:01:14.172
It's like a Khloe.

00:01:14.172 --> 00:01:16.205
- I could do without Gold, I think.

00:01:16.205 --> 00:01:18.295
(upbeat music)

00:01:18.295 --> 00:01:20.315
- Playfully spirited, charmingly fun,

00:01:20.315 --> 00:01:22.695
a bubbly, floral fruity that radiates

00:01:22.695 --> 00:01:24.634
a sunny and sparkling energy.

00:01:24.634 --> 00:01:26.874
Basically just described me.

00:01:26.874 --> 00:01:28.093
- It's like sweet and floral, it's like

00:01:28.093 --> 00:01:28.956
a honey flower.

00:01:28.956 --> 00:01:30.431
- Smells a lot like high school.

00:01:30.431 --> 00:01:32.577
- This could be like a
really good air freshener

00:01:32.577 --> 00:01:34.412
for after you make a shadoobs.

00:01:34.412 --> 00:01:36.652
- I like this one, this is nice.

00:01:36.652 --> 00:01:38.847
- Daisy, I think is the
perfect name for this.

00:01:38.847 --> 00:01:40.994
It's just like a good walk in the park.

00:01:40.994 --> 00:01:43.490
- If I were a girl, this
is what I would wear.

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:45.046
This is like Jewish girl from New York

00:01:45.046 --> 00:01:46.729
is probably all about this shit.

00:01:46.729 --> 00:01:49.712
(upbeat music)

00:01:49.712 --> 00:01:51.014
- Now this one I like.

00:01:51.014 --> 00:01:52.766
- I would be okay if my
girlfriend was wearing this.

00:01:52.766 --> 00:01:54.205
This is a nice smell.

00:01:54.205 --> 00:01:55.691
- I feel like she knows what she's doing,

00:01:55.691 --> 00:01:57.513
like, in the bedroom.

00:01:57.513 --> 00:01:58.849
And, like, at first, you're intimidated,

00:01:58.849 --> 00:02:00.265
you're like, "I don't know
if I can keep up with her,"

00:02:00.265 --> 00:02:01.809
and then she's like, "No, I got you.

00:02:01.809 --> 00:02:03.109
"I'ma teach you."

00:02:03.109 --> 00:02:07.266
- If you love taking Nyquil,
this is the perfume for you.

00:02:07.266 --> 00:02:09.645
- If somebody wore this and
was hugging me, I'd be like,

00:02:09.645 --> 00:02:11.270
"You smell nice, you smell good."

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:13.604
- I'm still at Daisy
level, but I hope some day,

00:02:13.604 --> 00:02:15.485
I could be La Vie Est Belle.

00:02:15.485 --> 00:02:16.458
(upbeat music)

00:02:16.458 --> 00:02:17.260
♫ Jazz. ♫

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:19.382
- Tom Ford.

00:02:19.382 --> 00:02:21.136
Tom Ford can do no wrong.

00:02:21.136 --> 00:02:23.383
- (sniffs)

00:02:23.575 --> 00:02:25.222
- Oh, that is, that is awful.

00:02:25.222 --> 00:02:26.257
- What is that?

00:02:26.257 --> 00:02:27.718
- No, get this one away.

00:02:27.718 --> 00:02:29.379
Smells like a churro died.

00:02:29.379 --> 00:02:31.840
- It smells like, uh, an Old Fashion.

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:33.523
- Like if an orange had an asshole.

00:02:33.523 --> 00:02:35.381
- This one actually smells like a dude.

00:02:35.381 --> 00:02:36.332
- Is it unisex?

00:02:36.332 --> 00:02:38.213
I feel like no sex should wear this one.

00:02:38.213 --> 00:02:39.199
- I'm not mad at it.

00:02:39.199 --> 00:02:40.117
I think I'd wear this one.

00:02:40.117 --> 00:02:42.438
I would wear this one whether
it was Tom Ford or not.

00:02:42.438 --> 00:02:43.994
- Who would wear this?

00:02:43.994 --> 00:02:46.978
If you're watching and you
wear this, I'm so sorry.

00:02:46.978 --> 00:02:48.499
We can never be.

00:02:48.499 --> 00:02:50.972
- You always notice when people smell bad.

00:02:50.972 --> 00:02:54.117
You don't necessarily notice
when people smell good.

00:02:54.117 --> 00:02:56.057
And so I think that's a good reason

00:02:56.057 --> 00:02:58.760
to invest into a nice cologne.

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:01.976
To be fair, you could probably
just go down to Rite-Aid.

00:03:01.976 --> 00:03:04.641
(squeaky sign swings)

